Report a write error on standard output at find -quit.
-quit called exit(), which flushes standard output without checking,
so names printed before -quit were lost without a message or a failure
status when they could not be written, as with "find . -print -quit
>/dev/full", while the same find without -quit reported the error. Exit
through fflush_stdout_and_exit(), as a normal return from find does.

---
 findutils/find.c |    2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/findutils/find.c
+++ b/findutils/find.c
@@ -948,7 +948,7 @@
 ACTF(quit)
 {
 	/* count the errors so far in the path being searched too */
-	exit(G.exitstatus | G.state->failed);
+	fflush_stdout_and_exit(G.exitstatus | G.state->failed);
 }
 #endif
 #if ENABLE_FEATURE_FIND_DELETE
